  "contract": [
    "Partition null yields count0; otherwise count=(partition.length>>12)&255. Partial sectors discarded and count deliberately truncated to a byte.",
    "Snapshot count before first command. For each index issue erase(partition.offset+(index<<12),4096), reloading live context partition/device and callback before each command.",
    "Continue through all sectors regardless of erase return status, as stock. Registered event calls the same erase implementation.",
    "No additional null guard is inferred for positive-count provider loss; valid live partition/device callbacks are required."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "FAL callbacks modeled, including negative/success return values and live offset/partition/device/size mutations; count256 and larger sizes exercise native byte truncation.",
    "Actual record-store parent assembly executes with the C count/erase functions; selection, fallback, writes and logging modeled.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, masks and caller stack guards checked. Private frames, incidental void registers and APSR excluded.",
    "Physical NOR erase, failures, concurrency, power-loss behavior, final application linking and boot remain unverified.",
    "This changes three entries in a partially assembly-based unit; other sleep storage assembly remains separate work."
